{
  "note": "v0.18.86 (J5b commission steps, owner 2026-11-13 ~20:48 UTC \"Yes, like this (Rec.)\", ~21:40 UTC \"Yes, warn (Rec.)\"; contract.json#commissionSteps): reference cases read by reference_check.py; the server and the admin (Pricing editor, Test a ride) use the same cases. validate: the admin's steps → \"ok\" or the first problem (400 invalid_request, reason commission_steps_invalid, details step:<index> / problem:<code>). pick: the step picked by the exact commission base (ride part + extras − waiting − stop waiting), the driver's ride part half_up to a minor unit (never below 0) and Movera's commission = base − that part. The key commission in these cases is the commission on the ride part only; it is not moneyBase.commission, which also holds the app fee, the pickup fee and the rounding. TND has 3 decimals (millimes). pick commissionBase.exact (optional, a decimal string) is the exact base before rounding when it is not a whole minor unit; then commission = exact base − driverRidePart, as a decimal string. warn (contract.json#commissionSteps.warn, ADVISORY: the admin warns and still saves; the server never refuses): for each limit L with a next step, a warning when the driver's ride part at base L (that step) is greater than at base L + 1 minor unit (the next step); { step, upToMinor, atLimit, justAbove } in minor units. The admin calculator (contract.json#commissionSteps.adminCalculator, owner ~22:46 UTC) must reproduce every pick and warn case here exactly; the J5b admin build replays them in a test. The test compares commission as a number (a decimal string when commissionBase.exact is given, an integer otherwise).",
